.TH TEXVIEW 1 "August 21, 1989"
.UC 4
.SH NAME
TeXview \- preview TeX dvi files on screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B TeXview
[
.B dvifile
]
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.I TeXview 
program displays dvi files generated by 
.I TeX 
on the NeXT
megapixel display.  The program is operated through menus and buttons
generated by 
.I Interface Builder.
.PP
Full support for 
.I PostScript 
fonts and graphics is supported in the
same manner as dvips(1).
.PP
Any missing fonts are generated automatically, unless this feature is
disabled from the Preferences menu item.  Missing fonts may also be
scaled from existing sizes.
.PP
A script for generating fonts is supplied in /usr/lib/tex/Make_Fonts;
it should be used to generate a base set of fonts for TeXview.
.PP
Note that this program will change directories to where the dvi file
is located so any included graphics files can be found.
.PP
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
This program uses the contents of two environment variables to search
for fonts.  The variable TEXPKS holds the colon-separated path to
search for pk files; its default value is
.PP
.ti+5n
 .:/LocalLibrary/Fonts/TeXFonts/pk:/usr/lib/tex/fonts/pk
.PP
The environment variable TEXFONTS holds the colon-separated path to
search for tfm files if a pk file cannot be found and font generation
is disabled; its default value is
.PP
.ti+5n
 .:/LocalLibrary/Fonts/TeXFonts/tfm:/usr/lib/tex/fonts/tfm
.PP
.SH FILES
.PP
.ti+5n
 /usr/lib/tex/fonts/pk        
.ti+25n
Where pk bitmap fonts are stored
.ti+5n
 /NextLibrary/Fonts/TeXFonts  
.ti+25n 
A link to /usr/lib/tex/fonts
.ti+5n
 /LocalLibrary/Fonts/TeXFonts 
.ti+5n
 /usr/bin/MakeTeXPK           
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
tex(1), dvips(1), mf(1)
.PP
.SH BUGS
Three forms of specials must appear on the first page of the document if
they are to be recognized; these are the landscape special, any header
file specials, and any literal macro (exclamation point) specials.  Refer
to the dvips(1) man page for more information on these specials.
